edition 5;

module ml.spec;

// What `ml` says about itself: the flag table that drives the parser, `introspect` and `skill` (cancho docs/agent-toolbox.md
// D11), the rules of its own beside the shared catalogue, and the log records. Three tables, each written once; the schemas
// (scripts/schemas.py), the fixtures (tests/fixtures/cli.json) and the gates (tests/conformance/test_tables.py) are checked
// against them, so a flag, a rule or a log record that is in one place and not in the others fails the build.
//
// Format: entries separated by `;`, fields by `|`, so no help text holds either character.

import toolbox.describe;

// name|short|kind|role|default|help
pub fn flag_table() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "root||path|root||resolve FILE, --model-file, --output and --log beneath this directory, following no symbolic link, and refuse paths outside it;{{MODEL_FLAG}}plan||path|path-read||fit: a plan text file (steps and a final model line, docs/pipeline.md section 2) for a model other than constant. It is the one description of the fit: --model, --step, --task and the hyperparameter flags are then args.conflict. The canonical plan is stored in the model file;step||text|none||fit: the steps of the pipeline of a model other than constant, written verb key=value as in a plan, several separated by semicolons (ASCII 59), for example impute column=* strategy=mean then scale column=a,b kind=standard. The flag may be given once. The model line is built from --model and the hyperparameter flags;{{HYPER_FLAGS}}positive||text|none||fit, eval: the positive label of a classification (logistic, tree or forest). fit: the label whose probability the model predicts (default: the larger of the two labels). eval: the label that precision, recall, F1, ROC-AUC and log-loss are about (default: the model's own);split||text|none||fit, eval: train=F with 0 < F < 1 (at most 6 digits after the point). fit trains on the train rows and reports the held-out rows. eval scores the test rows only. The rows are chosen by the seeded train/test split of lib/metrics (--seed), the test side being ceil(n * (1 - F)) rows;seed||nat|none|0|fit, eval: the seed of --split (the stream registry, kind 4), of the bootstrap and feature draws of a tree or forest (kinds 1 and 2) and of the initial centres of kmeans (kind 3): one flag, so a forest fitted with --split draws its bootstrap from the seed that chose the split. Stored in the model file;stratify||bool|none||fit, eval, cv: hold the rows out (or deal them into folds) so that each class keeps its share: with --split, per class the held-out rows are the floor or the ceiling of its exact share, and with cv, per class and fold the count is the floor or the ceiling of the class size over --folds. A classification target only (ml.split.stratify-target otherwise). Not with --split-by or --split-group (ml.split.combination);split-by||text|none||fit, eval, cv: time:COLUMN orders the rows by COLUMN, a number or an ISO-8601 date or datetime (YYYY-MM-DD, then T or a space, hh:mm, optional :ss, optional .fraction of 1 to 9 digits, optional Z, no numeric offset). With --split the oldest train=F of the rows train and the newest test, and with cv the rows are cut into folds+1 blocks and fold i trains on blocks 0 to i and tests on block i+1 (an expanding window). Ties keep the order of the file. A text column needs --drop. Not with --stratify or --split-group;split-group||text|none||fit, eval, cv: COLUMN names a column (text or integer) whose values are groups: all the rows of a group are on one side of --split, or in one fold of cv. Groups are compared byte for byte and assigned by the seeded stream. A text column needs --drop. Not with --stratify or --split-by;folds||nat|none|5|cv: the number of folds, 2 to 20 (ml.split.out-of-range outside);repeats||nat|none|1|cv: how many times the fold assignment is drawn again with the next index of the stream, 1 to 10. The mean and the standard deviation are over all folds of all repeats. Not above 1 with --split-by;emit-folds||bool|none||fit, eval, cv: put the assignment of the rows in the answer: for each row (in file order) the fold, or 0 for a train row and 1 for a held-out row of --split. At most 1048576 entries (ml.split.emit-too-large);threads||nat|none|1|fit, eval, runs verify: the threads of the numeric kernels, 1 to 64 (ml.param.threads outside). No thread count changes a byte of the model file or of the answer. In eval nothing is threaded and the flag is checked and unused. In runs verify it is the thread count of the refit;proba||bool|none||predict: add the probability column (the positive label's probability) to the answer of a classification model (logistic, tree or forest);distance||bool|none||predict: add the distance column (the squared Euclidean distance of the row to the centre of its cluster) to the answer of a kmeans model;task||choice:regression/classification|none|regression|what the target column is: a number to predict (regression) or a label with exactly two values (classification). It is also the task of a tree or forest, which serve both and never guess it from the target. kmeans is a clustering and takes no task;target||text|none||fit: the name of the column to predict, as the header spells it. Every model but kmeans needs it, and kmeans has no target and refuses the flag (args.conflict);drop||text|none||columns to ignore, header names separated by commas (fit, predict, eval). A dropped column is not part of the stored schema, and its cells are not read as numbers (it may hold text, quoted fields and line breaks);float||text|none||fit: columns to read as floating point whatever their cells are, header names separated by commas. A column with an exponent, a leading or trailing point or more than 12 digits is a float without being named. A float is read to the nearest double, ties to even, by cancho-table's exact reader (pinned, not copied). On a float target the constant is the exact sum of the doubles over the count, rounded once;cat||text|none||fit: columns to read as categorical text, header names separated by commas (docs/categorical.md). Every cell of such a column is a string, compared byte for byte: no case folding, no trimming, no Unicode normalisation, and it must be well-formed UTF-8. The distinct strings of a column are kept in a dictionary sorted bytewise (the id of a string is its rank), so the result does not depend on the order of the rows or on --threads. An empty cell and a cell equal to a --na-values marker are missing. A text column that is not named here is refused (ml.input.non-numeric). The target, a dropped column and a --float column cannot be named. The columns are encoded by the steps encode, freq and hash of a planned model (docs/categorical-encoders.md). A declared column that no step reads is refused with ml.input.categorical-not-encoded. The model file stores the training strings of every encoded column (a hash step stores none), so predict and eval read the columns by name from the file alone;na-values||text|none||fit, with --cat: strings that mean missing in a categorical column besides the empty cell, separated by commas (so a marker holds no comma), for example NA,?. At most 64 markers of 1 to 255 bytes. A marker is compared with the whole cell, byte for byte, after unquoting. Numeric columns are not affected;max-categories||nat|none|64|fit, with --cat: the most distinct values in one categorical column, 1 to 1024. More is ml.limit.categories, at the value that passes the limit, before anything is stored for it;max-string-bytes||nat|none|255|fit, with --cat: the longest cell of a categorical column in bytes, 1 to 65536. A longer one is ml.limit.string-bytes;max-pool-bytes||nat|none|1048576|fit, with --cat: the most bytes of all the distinct categories of all the categorical columns together, 1 to 8388608. More is ml.limit.string-pool;max-cat-columns||nat|none|128|fit, with --cat: the most categorical columns, 1 to 4096. More is ml.limit.categorical-columns, before the file is read past its header;output||path|path-write||fit: where to write the model file. The directory must exist. An existing file is refused unless --overwrite;model-file||path|path-read||predict, eval, describe: the model file to read;overwrite||bool|guard||fit: replace an existing --output. The new file is written beside it under a temporary name and renamed over it, so a reader never sees half a file;dry-run||bool|guard||fit: read, check and fit, then report what would be written (planned_actions) and exit 9, writing nothing;limit||nat|none|1000|predict: the most rows in one page of predictions, at least 1. describe: the most category strings listed for each categorical column, at least 1. runs list: the most run records listed, at least 1;from||nat|none|0|predict: the row to start the page at, counting data rows from 0;max-rows||nat|none|10000000|the most data rows read. More is ml.input.too-many-rows;max-columns||nat|none|4096|the most columns read. More is ml.input.too-many-columns;max-cells||nat|none|400000000|the most rows times columns. More is ml.input.too-many-cells;max-line-bytes||nat|none|1048576|the longest line read. A longer one is limit.line-too-long;max-bytes||nat|none|16777216|fit: the largest model file written, the limit predict and eval apply when they read it. A larger one is limit.input-too-large and nothing is written. predict, eval, describe: the largest model file read. A larger one is limit.input-too-large. predict from standard input (the operand - or none): the CSV is held in memory, so this is also the most bytes of standard input read. More is limit.input-too-large;track||path|path-write||fit, eval: write a run record into this directory, beneath --root (docs/tracking.md). The directory must exist. fit writes DIR/RUNID.json, a canonical JSON record of the inputs that determine the model (the training file's SHA-256 and size, the plan, the seed, the split, the compiler pin, never the thread count), the model file's name, size and SHA-256 and the metrics, with no timestamp, no host name and no payload. The run id is the SHA-256 of the inputs, so the same inputs write the same record and an existing record that differs is ml.runs.conflict. eval writes DIR/RUNID.eval-SCOREDSHA.json beside the run of the model file. At most 1000 records of at most 262144 bytes;max-out-of-range||nat|none||predict, eval: refuse with ml.predict.out-of-range when more than N rows hold a non-missing numeric feature strictly below the minimum or above the maximum of the training rows, as stored in the model file (0 refuses any). Absent, the counts are reported and no bound applies. A model file with no provenance section (fitted before run tracking) refuses the flag with ml.predict.no-provenance;log||path|path-write||append NDJSON records of this run to this file. Records hold counts, rule tags and hashes, never a cell, a column name or a path;log-max-bytes||nat|none|1048576|refuse to log into a file already this long (limit.log-full). The log of one run adds at most 2048 bytes;format||choice:json/text|none|json|json: one document on one line. text: a few lines for a person, errors as sentences on standard error";
}

// tag|exit|repairable|summary. The shared catalogue (toolbox.rules) has args.*, path.*, io.*, limit.line-too-long,
// limit.input-too-large, conflict.exists and path.bad-name; these are ml's own. Summaries end `Hint: ... Repair: ...`.
pub fn extra() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "ml.predict.out-of-range|8|never|more rows hold a numeric feature outside the range the model was fitted on than --max-out-of-range allows. The number of rows, the bound, the first column and the first row are in detail. Hint: check where the data comes from, or raise --max-out-of-range. Repair: none.;ml.predict.no-provenance|8|never|--max-out-of-range was given and the model file has no provenance section (it was fitted before run tracking), so no range is known. Hint: refit the model with this version of ml. Repair: none.;ml.runs.conflict|8|never|a run record with this id exists and differs from the one this call would write in more than the thread count: the same inputs gave another model, or the record was edited. Hint: compare them with ml runs compare, and let only ml write the directory. Repair: none.;ml.runs.too-many|8|never|the --track directory already holds 1000 run records. Hint: track into another directory. Repair: none.;ml.runs.record-too-large|8|never|the run record would be longer than 262144 bytes. Hint: shorten the plan or the column lists. Repair: none.;ml.runs.not-found|3|never|no run record of the directory has this id. Hint: ml runs list names the ids. Repair: none.;ml.runs.unknown-model|8|never|no run record of the --track directory holds the SHA-256 of this model file. Hint: track the fit with ml fit --track first. Repair: none.;ml.runs.damaged|8|never|a file of the runs directory is not a run record of this version: it does not parse, a member is outside its bound, or its id is not the hash of its inputs. The file is in detail. Hint: do not edit the records, restore the file. Repair: none.;ml.runs.data-changed|8|never|the training file the record names does not have the SHA-256 the record holds. The two hashes are in detail. Hint: restore the file the record names. Repair: none.;ml.runs.model-differs|8|never|the refit gave a model file whose SHA-256 is not the record's. The two hashes and the two compiler pins are in detail. Hint: a record is replayable by the compiler it names. Repair: none.;ml.runs.not-replayable|8|never|the record cannot be refitted by ml runs verify: a column carrying --drop, --float or --cat is past the 62nd position of the header. The column is in detail. Hint: refit by hand with the flags of the record. Repair: none.;args.unknown-command|2|never|the first operand is not fit, predict or eval. Hint: the verbs are fit, predict and eval, and ml introspect and ml skill describe them. Repair: none.;ml.param.out-of-range|2|never|a numeric flag is below its minimum or above its ceiling. Hint: the range is in detail and in introspect limits. Repair: none.;ml.input.empty|8|never|the file has a header and no data rows. Hint: give a file with at least one data row. Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-rows|8|never|more data rows than --max-rows, or more training rows than the 1048576 a tree or forest fit takes (a boosted fit too: the bound of the tree's exact Gini comparison). Hint: raise --max-rows up to its ceiling, or fit on a sample of the rows (a tree, forest or boost: at most 1048576 training rows, also with --split). Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-columns|8|never|more columns than --max-columns. Hint: raise --max-columns up to its ceiling, or drop columns with --drop. Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-cells|8|never|rows times columns is more than --max-cells. Hint: raise --max-cells up to its ceiling, or use fewer rows or columns. Repair: none.;ml.input.non-numeric|8|sometimes|a cell of a kept column is not a number, or is empty. A number is an integer, a decimal, or a float (an exponent, a leading or trailing point, more than 12 digits). A non-zero cell that would read as zero, and a cell longer than 1100 bytes, are refused with this tag. The line, the column and the reason are in detail. Hint: drop the column with --drop, or fix the cell. A text column the model should keep is declared with --cat (fit). Repair: retry.;ml.input.non-finite|8|never|a cell is nan or inf, or a number past the range of a double. Hint: remove the row or the column. Repair: none.;ml.input.duplicate-column|8|never|two columns have the same header name, or a column name is empty. Hint: rename the columns in the file. Repair: none.;ml.input.unknown-column|3|never|--target or --drop names a column that is not in the header. Hint: names are compared exactly, byte for byte. Repair: none.;parse.csv-ragged-row|8|never|a data row has a different number of fields from the header. The line is in detail. Hint: fix the row. Repair: none.;parse.csv-bad-quote|8|never|a closing quote is followed by something other than a comma or the end of the record. The line is in detail. Hint: double a quote that is text, or put the comma after the closing quote. Repair: none.;parse.csv-unterminated-quote|8|never|a quoted field is still open at the end of the file. The line where its record began is in detail. Hint: close the quote, or double the quotes that are text. Repair: none.;ml.label.single-class|8|never|a classification target has one value. Hint: a model needs both classes in the training rows. Repair: none.;ml.label.not-binary|8|never|a classification target has more than two values. Hint: only two-class targets are built. Repair: none.;ml.label.not-integer|8|never|a classification target is not an integer column. Hint: label the classes with integers. Repair: none.;ml.schema.mismatch|8|sometimes|the input columns differ from the fitted schema: missing, extra or of another type. They are named in detail. Hint: the missing columns must be added. Extra columns can be ignored with --drop. Repair: retry.;ml.model.bad-magic|8|never|the file does not start with CML1. Hint: this is not a cancho-ml model file. Repair: none.;ml.model.version|8|never|the file has a format version this reader does not know, or a model of kind 4 to 8 made with a summation order this reader does not implement (sum_order and known in detail). Hint: refit with this version of ml. Repair: none.;ml.model.truncated|8|never|the file ends before the end the header and the section lengths promise, or a length runs past the end. Hint: copy the file again. Repair: none.;ml.model.checksum|8|never|the SHA-256 at the end of the file is not the hash of the bytes before it. Hint: the file changed after it was written. Repair: none.;ml.metric.undefined|8|never|the sum of squared errors of a float regression is beyond the largest double. Hint: scale the target down. Repair: none.;ml.model.malformed|8|never|the file passes the checksum but a section is not what the format allows. The section is in detail. Hint: refit. Repair: none.;limit.log-full|8|never|the --log file is already --log-max-bytes long. Hint: move the log away, or raise --log-max-bytes. Repair: none.;ml.linalg.not-positive-definite|8|never|a Cholesky pivot is not above 2^-40 times its own diagonal element (dependent or nearly dependent columns, or not positive, NaN included). Hint: set l2 above 2^-40 times the diagonal (n for standardised features), drop one of the dependent columns, or centre and scale the columns. Repair: none.;ml.param.threads|2|never|a thread count outside 1 to 64, or a tree fit whose thread copies would not fit the memory ceiling. Hint: give a thread count of 1 to 64. Repair: none.;ml.fit.non-finite|8|never|a coefficient, a loss or a gain became non-finite during a fit. Hint: scale the features, add l2, or use fewer iterations. Repair: none.;ml.predict.non-finite|8|never|a prediction, a probability or a squared distance of a row is NaN or infinite, which no answer can write as a number. The row of the file (1-based) and the column of the answer are in detail. Hint: scale the inputs, or check or drop the row. Repair: none.;ml.split.empty-fold|8|never|k is larger than the number of rows, or a train/test split would leave a side empty. Hint: use fewer folds or a smaller test size. Repair: none.;ml.split.stratify-target|2|always|--stratify needs a classification target: a regression or a clustering has no classes to keep in proportion. Hint: drop --stratify, or use --task classification with a model that has a class target. Repair: retry without --stratify.;ml.split.stratum-too-small|8|sometimes|a class has fewer rows than the split needs (fewer than --folds for cv, fewer than 2 for --split, or a class that would have no training row). Hint: use fewer folds, or more rows of the rare class. Repair: retry with --folds set to the rows of the smallest class when that is at least 2.;ml.split.too-few-groups|8|sometimes|the group column has fewer groups than --folds (cv), or fewer than 2 (--split). Hint: use fewer folds, or a column with more groups. Repair: retry with --folds set to the number of groups when that is at least 2.;ml.split.time-format|8|never|a cell of the --split-by column is not a number or an accepted ISO-8601 date or datetime, or is of the other kind than the first cell (row, column and reason in detail: not-a-time, form, offset, range, mixed). Hint: write YYYY-MM-DD, optionally with T or a space and hh:mm[:ss[.fraction]][Z], or numbers, and convert an offset to UTC first. Repair: none.;ml.split.missing-cell|8|never|a cell of the --split-by or --split-group column is empty (row and column in detail). Hint: fill the cell or remove the row: a row with no time or no group cannot be placed. Repair: none.;ml.split.combination|2|sometimes|two options that cannot be given together: --stratify, --split-group and --split-by are different algorithms, cv takes no --split, --repeats above 1 has no meaning for --split-by, and --early-stopping validates on a random tenth of the training rows, which a group or a time split does not allow. Hint: keep one of them. Repair: retry with --repeats 1 when that is the conflict, retry without --early-stopping when that is, else none.;ml.split.out-of-range|2|never|--folds outside 2 to 20, or --repeats outside 1 to 10. Hint: the range is in detail. Repair: none.;ml.split.column-target|2|never|the --split-group or --split-by column is the target. Hint: name another column: a split rule built on the target would leak it. Repair: none.;ml.split.emit-too-large|8|always|--emit-folds would put more than 1048576 entries (rows times repeats) in the answer. Hint: drop --emit-folds, or use fewer repeats or rows. Repair: retry without --emit-folds.;ml.fit.all-missing|8|never|a selected column has no non-missing cell in the training rows (every transform but impute strategy=constant). Hint: drop the column, or impute with a constant. Repair: none.;ml.limit.categories|8|never|a column has more distinct values than max-categories. Hint: raise max-categories up to 1024, or bucket the column. Repair: none.;ml.limit.string-bytes|8|never|a cell of a categorical column (--cat) is longer than --max-string-bytes. The line, the column, the length and the limit are in detail. Hint: raise --max-string-bytes up to 65536, or drop the column. Repair: none.;ml.limit.string-pool|8|never|the distinct categories of all the categorical columns together would take more than --max-pool-bytes. The line, the column, the size and the limit are in detail. Hint: raise --max-pool-bytes up to 8388608, or drop a column with long or many categories. Repair: none.;ml.limit.categorical-columns|8|never|more columns are named by --cat than --max-cat-columns. Seen at the header, before any row. Hint: raise --max-cat-columns up to 4096, or name fewer columns. Repair: none.;ml.input.invalid-utf8|8|never|a cell of a categorical column (--cat) is not well-formed UTF-8: an overlong form, a surrogate, a code point past U+10FFFF or a truncated sequence. The line, the column, the name and the offset of the first bad byte in the cell are in detail. Hint: re-encode the file as UTF-8 (for Latin-1 text: iconv -f latin1 -t utf-8), or remove the column from --cat and drop it. Repair: none.;ml.input.categorical-not-encoded|8|never|a column named by --cat is read by no step of the plan, so the fit would drop it silently. The names of those columns, the number of categories of each and the SHA-256 of the canonical dump of the reader's vocabulary are in detail. Hint: name the column in an encode, freq or hash step (for example encode column=NAME kind=onehot), or remove it from --cat and drop it with --drop. Repair: none.;ml.plan.column-kind|8|sometimes|a step reads the other kind of column than the one it names: a numeric step (impute, scale, bucket) on a categorical column, freq or hash on a numeric column, a list that mixes the two, or min-count or missing on numeric columns. The step, the column and what the step needs are in detail. Hint: encode the categorical column first (encode column=NAME kind=onehot), or name columns of the kind the step reads. Repair: retry.;ml.input.reserved-category|8|never|min-count is 2 or more and a categorical column holds the value __other__, the name of the rare-category bucket. The step and the column are in detail. Hint: rename that value in the file, or use min-count=1. Repair: none.;ml.model.string-table|8|never|the string table of a model file (the fitted vocabulary of its categorical steps) is damaged, passes a bound, or disagrees with the steps, the plan or the schema of its own file. The reason, the step and the section are in detail. Hint: refit the model, or copy the file again. Repair: none.;ml.limit.string-table|8|never|the categories of the fitted steps would make a string table over its bounds (131072 strings, 8 MiB of string bytes, 12 MiB in all). What passed, its size and the maximum are in detail. Hint: encode fewer or shorter categories, or hash the column with a hash step, which stores none. Repair: none.;ml.input.unknown-category|8|never|an encode step with unknown=refuse met a value no training row had. Hint: refit with the value in the training rows, or use unknown=ignore. Repair: none.;ml.plan.syntax|8|never|a plan line is not verb key=value (line and column are in detail). Hint: one step per line, verb key=value. Repair: none.;ml.plan.unknown-step|8|never|the verb of a plan line is not impute, scale, encode, bucket, freq, hash or model. Hint: use one of the seven verbs. Repair: none.;ml.plan.unknown-key|8|never|a key the verb does not take. Hint: see the keys of the verb in docs/pipeline.md. Repair: none.;ml.plan.missing-key|8|never|a required key of the verb is absent. Hint: add the key. Repair: none.;ml.plan.bad-value|8|never|a value that is not in the key's list or not a number of the key's kind. Hint: see the values of the key in docs/pipeline.md. Repair: none.;ml.plan.duplicate-key|8|never|the same key twice on one line. Hint: write each key once. Repair: none.;ml.plan.model-line|8|never|the plan has no model line, two, or a step after it. Hint: end the plan with exactly one model line. Repair: none.;ml.plan.unknown-column|8|never|a column named by a step is not a column of the matrix the step receives. Hint: names are compared byte for byte. Repair: none.;ml.limit.plan|8|never|the plan has more bytes, lines or listed columns than the limits. Hint: at most 64 KiB, 64 lines, 4096 names in a list. Repair: none.;ml.input.missing-value|8|sometimes|a feature cell is empty and no impute step of the plan covers its column (the columns are in detail). Hint: add an impute step for the columns, for example impute column=a,b strategy=mean. Repair: retry when no plan or step was given.;ml.plan.model-not-built|8|never|the model line of the plan names a model ml does not build (constant, which takes no plan). Hint: use linear, logistic, kmeans, tree or forest in a plan, or --model constant without one. Repair: none.;ml.limit.depth|8|never|a tree, forest or boost over the depth ceiling (30). Hint: give a max-depth of at most 30. Repair: none.;ml.limit.nodes|8|never|a tree, forest or boost over the node ceiling: max-nodes above 4194304, trees times the nodes a tree can have above 16777216 (boost: rounds times the nodes a tree can have above 4194304), or a tree that needs more nodes than max-nodes (it is never cut). Hint: raise --max-nodes up to 4194304, lower --max-depth, --trees or --rounds, or raise --min-leaf. Repair: none.";
}

// The rules of the libraries that no input can make `ml` answer (docs/wiring.md section 5): descriptors the wiring builds from a validated shape
// (ml.tensor.*), a triangular solve the relative pivot test never lets reach a zero (ml.linalg.singular), metrics given arrays of one length and
// probabilities in [0, 1] by construction (ml.metric.length-mismatch, bad-probability), trees and the stratified split (not wired). Same convention as
// extra(). They are NOT in rules(), so not in `introspect`, in the schemas or among the fixtures: a rule in the table is a promise that a fixture
// reaches it. The tags the verbs can reach moved to extra() and rules() at the wiring stage (docs/integration.md). The tags of the libraries that ml does reach (ml.input.*, ml.label.*, ml.schema.mismatch, ml.model.*,
// ml.metric.undefined, ml.param.out-of-range) are in extra() already. scripts/check_registry.py compares this table with the libraries'
// tag tables (lib/core/refuse.cho, lib/metrics/rules.cho, lib/models/tree/deny.cho) and with design.md section 8.
pub fn pending() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "ml.tensor.rank|8|never|a tensor of rank 0 or above 4 was given to a kernel. Hint: use a tensor of rank 1 to 4 (rank 1 and 2 have kernels). Repair: none.;ml.tensor.shape|8|never|an extent below 1, or a reshape of a tensor that is not contiguous. Hint: give every extent as an integer of at least 1, and reshape only a contiguous tensor to the same element count. Repair: none.;ml.tensor.bounds|8|never|the offset, shape and strides of a descriptor reach outside the data given beside it. Hint: they must stay inside the data. Repair: none.;ml.linalg.singular|8|never|a zero on the diagonal of a triangular solve. Hint: the matrix has no inverse. Repair: none.;ml.metric.length-mismatch|8|never|two arrays of a metric have different lengths. Hint: give one prediction per row. Repair: none.;ml.metric.bad-probability|8|never|a probability outside 0 to 1. Hint: log-loss needs the probability of the positive class. Repair: none.";
}

