runs.not-replayable";
}

// the flags each verb takes, comma separated. A flag of the table that a verb does not list is args.conflict with that verb;
// every flag of the table is listed by at least one verb (tests/conformance/test_tables.py).
pub fn allowed(verb: int) -> [] &static [byte] {
    if verb == 1 {
        return "root,model,task,target,drop,float,cat,na-values,max-categories,max-string-bytes,max-pool-bytes,max-cat-columns,output,overwrite,dry-run,plan,step{{HYPER_ALLOW}},positive,split,seed,threads,stratify,split-by,split-group,emit-folds,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,max-bytes,track,log,log-max-bytes,format";
    }
    if verb == 2 {
        return "root,model-file,drop,limit,from,proba,distance,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,max-bytes,max-out-of-range,log,log-max-bytes,format";
    }
    if verb == 4 {
        return "root,model-file,limit,max-bytes,format";
    }
    if verb == 5 {
        return "root,model,task,target,drop,float,cat,na-values,max-categories,max-string-bytes,max-pool-bytes,max-cat-columns,plan,step{{HYPER_ALLOW}},positive,split,seed,threads,stratify,split-by,split-group,folds,repeats,emit-folds,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,max-bytes,log,log-max-bytes,format";
    }
    if verb == 6 {
        return "root,limit,threads,max-bytes,format";
    }
    return "root,model-file,drop,positive,split,seed,threads,stratify,split-by,split-group,emit-folds,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,max-bytes,max-out-of-range,track,log,log-max-bytes,format";
}

// event|fields. The records of the NDJSON log (--log). Each is one line, a closed object; a field is a count, a flag, a
// rule tag or a hash, never data. `seq` is the position in the run.
pub fn log_table() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "start|event,seq,command,version;read|event,seq,rows,columns,bytes;write|event,seq,bytes,sha256;end|event,seq,ok,exit,rule";
}

// name|default|ceiling
pub fn limits() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "limit|1000|1000000;from|0|1000000000;max-rows|10000000|1000000000;max-columns|4096|8192;max-cells|400000000|1099511627776;max-line-bytes|1048576|16777216;max-bytes|16777216|268435456;log-max-bytes|1048576|1073741824;max-categories|64|1024;max-string-bytes|255|65536;max-pool-bytes|1048576|8388608;max-cat-columns|128|4096;max-out-of-range|0|1000000000{{LIMITS_HYPER}}";
}

pub fn tool() -> [] describe.Tool {
    return describe.Tool { name: "ml", version: "0.1.0", summary: "Fit, apply and score a model on a CSV file, with the refusals of a tool an agent can read. Models: {{MODEL_LIST}}. constant is the baseline: for a regression the training mean, for a classification the majority class and its probability. linear (least squares, ridge with --l2), logistic (Newton's method), tree (a CART decision tree with histogram splits), forest (bagged trees, parallel over trees; --task, --trees, --max-depth, --seed) and kmeans (a clustering with no target: --k centres, a fixed number of Lloyd iterations, a seeded initialisation; it needs no --target and refuses missing cells) are fitted through a pipeline of steps (impute, scale, encode, bucket) given by --step or --plan, fitted on the training rows and stored with the estimator in ONE model file, so predict and eval apply exactly the fitted steps (a tree or forest takes missing cells itself and learns a default side per split; the others need an impute step) and there is no way to predict with another transformation. fit reads a CSV (integer, decimal and floating-point columns, RFC 4180 quoting; an empty cell is a missing value that the plan must impute) and writes a model file (CML1: sections, tensor records, a SHA-256 trailer). predict applies the stored schema, steps and model to another CSV (--proba adds the probability of a classification model, --distance the squared distance of a row to its cluster centre for kmeans). eval scores a model on a CSV: for constant, accuracy from exact counts or the exact sum of squared errors with the RMSE; for linear, RMSE, MAE and R2; for logistic, tree and forest classifications, accuracy, precision, recall, F1, ROC-AUC and log-loss (the positive label is --positive), and for their regressions RMSE, MAE and R2; for kmeans, the inertia, the cluster sizes and the mean distance of each cluster. --split train=F --seed N holds rows out by the seeded split of the metrics library; --threads N sets the threads of fit and changes no byte. The same input, plan and seed give the same model bytes at any thread count. Every refusal is a rule tag with its hint. Verbs: fit FILE (--target, --output; --model, --plan, --step, {{HYPER_FLAG_NAMES}}, --positive, --split, --seed, --threads, --task, --drop, --float, --cat, --na-values, --overwrite, --dry-run, --max-bytes), predict FILE or predict - (--model-file; --proba, --distance, --drop, --limit, --from; - or no FILE reads standard input), eval FILE (--model-file; --positive, --split, --seed, --threads, --drop, and the holdout rules of fit: --stratify, --split-by, --split-group, --emit-folds), cv FILE (--target; the model flags of fit; --folds, --repeats, --seed, --stratify, --split-by, --split-group, --emit-folds: scores a model by k-fold cross-validation, fitting every step on the training rows of each fold only, and writes no file), describe (--model-file; --limit: what the model file requires of a caller, as data), runs list DIR, runs show DIR ID, runs compare DIR ID ID and runs verify DIR ID (the run records of --track, docs/tracking.md). The first operand is the verb, the second the CSV file. Every model file carries the SHA-256 and size of the training file and the range of each numeric feature (a provenance section): eval says whether it scored the training file (on), and predict and eval count the cells outside the range (out_of_range, bounded by --max-out-of-range).", usage: "fit:     ml [--root DIR] [--model {{MODEL_CHOICES}}] [--plan PLAN | --step STEPS] {{HYPER_USAGE}} [--positive LABEL] [--split train=F] [--seed N] [--threads N] [--task regression|classification] [--target NAME] --output MODEL [--drop NAMES] [--float NAMES] [--overwrite] [--dry-run] [--max-rows N] [--max-columns N] [--max-cells N] [--max-line-bytes N] [--max-bytes N] [--track DIR] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] fit FILE\npredict: ml [--root DIR] --model-file MODEL [--proba] [--distance] [--drop NAMES] [--limit N] [--from N] [--max-bytes N] [--max-out-of-range N] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] predict FILE|-\ndescribe: ml [--root DIR] --model-file MODEL [--limit N] [--max-bytes N] [--format json|text] describe\ncv:      ml [--root DIR] [--model {{MODEL_CHOICES}}] [--plan PLAN | --step STEPS] [--target NAME] [--folds K] [--repeats R] [--stratify | --split-group COLUMN | --split-by time:COLUMN] [--emit-folds] [--seed N] [--threads N] [--drop NAMES] [--format json|text] cv FILE\neval:    ml [--root DIR] --model-file MODEL [--positive LABEL] [--split train=F] [--seed N] [--threads N] [--drop NAMES] [--max-bytes N] [--max-out-of-range N] [--track DIR] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] eval FILE\nruns:    ml [--root DIR] [--limit N] [--threads N] [--max-bytes N] [--format json|text] runs list DIR | runs show DIR ID | runs compare DIR ID ID | runs verify DIR ID\n\nFILE: a CSV with a header row, comma separated, RFC 4180 quoting, a byte order mark, CRLF and blank lines read. Cells are integers, decimals or floating-point numbers; nan and inf are refused; an empty cell is refused by constant and is a missing value for the pipeline models (impute it). Paths are relative to --root when given. predict reads standard input for the operand - or for no operand (--root does not apply to it).", output: "document", schema: "ml.v1", flags: flag_table(), operands: "VERB|none|1|1|fit, predict, eval, cv, describe or runs;FILE|path-read|0|1|the CSV file to read (predict: - or no operand is standard input; describe takes none; runs takes list, show, compare or verify and then the directory DIR of run records and the ids), a path relative to --root when given (absolute paths, .. and symbolic links are refused), whose first row is the header", rules: rules(), extra_rules: extra(), limits: limits(), reversibility: "irreversible-bounded", stdin: "predict reads the CSV from standard input when FILE is - or absent", guarantees: "deterministic;idempotent;dry_run" };
